ary extraction distinguishes a read that failed from a subject that is empty.\n\n## What happens today\n\nThe run locates a concern in its home graph by name and by the file that holds it. A file does not separate one symbol of a name from another: a type and its implementation block share one, and a tree that mirrors a type into a second crate carries several more. Where a name reaches more than one symbol, the graph reads answer with the candidates instead of a report, so the run measures no radius at all and the boundary it extracts is drawn from nothing. Both operations it binds have always declared an input that reaches one symbol and no other; the run never passed it.\n\nThe boundary extraction also reads two states where the tools produce three. An inventory that comes back empty adds no entry, and so does one that comes back an error, so a tree that serves no route and a read that failed leave the same trace.\n\n## The change\n\nThe run declares the concern's identity and binds it to both home reads — the connections read and the radius read — so a name that reaches several symbols is resolved to the one the caller means. The input it replaces named a file, which cannot do that job, and the declaration says so.\n\nBoundary extraction names the third state. An errored inventory is recorded as unmeasured, beside the kinds that came back empty, because only the record separates a read that failed from a subject with nothing to report. A radius that came back as candidates adds no entry either, for the same reason it measured nothing.\n\nThe specimen carries the identity through its variable, its activity and its orienting prose.\n\n## What was verified\n\nThe full corpus guard sweep over this branch passes, 49 guards, under engine `main`. On the experiment sidecar serving this branch, the minimum viable workflow walked first, then the specimen walked to completion over a six-member group: the identity resolved a single symbol in both home reads where the bare name reaches four, the home tree's route inventory failed on that graph and is recorded as unmeasured, four members settled from the group registry, one from a search of its tree, and the member carrying no graph from the registry alone. Every row names its graph and the instruments that answered.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo change to the reach judgement's instruments or to their precedence; no engine or schema change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T17:11:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T12:45:56Z","closed_at":"2026-09-22T17:11:44Z","merged_at":"2026-09-22T17:11:44Z","merge_commit_sha":"ecd5b2278952212c64fad9bffb002dfa56be0b4c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"m2ux:workflow/881-gitnexus-group-radius","ref":"workflow/881-gitnexus-group-radius","repo":{"id":1137318642,"node_id":"R_kgDOQ8oa8g","name":"workflow-server","full_name":"m2ux/workflow-server","owner":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"A M